        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ead744da-07b3-57a2-99f2-bda1efe3662d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Characters: Space Ghost, Zorak, Brak, Moltar\n- People: Andy Merrill, C. Martin Croker, Don Messick\n- Series and Productions: Space Ghost, Space Ghost Coast to Coast, Cartoon Planet, Space Ghost's Musical Bar-B-Que\n- Companies: Hanna-Barbera, Cartoon Network\n- Roles: voice actor, writer, producer, supervillain, space pirate\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1966 Hanna-Barbera animated series \"Space Ghost,\" Brak is a fictional supervillain portrayed as a catlike alien space pirate trying to conquer the galaxy.\n- Don Messick originally voiced Zorak and Moltar in the 1960s series \"Space Ghost.\"\n- Andy Ronald Merrill was born on November 27, 1966, in Newark, Ohio.\n- Andy Merrill is an American television writer, producer, and voice actor best known for his comedy voice portrayal of Brak on \"Space Ghost Coast to Coast,\" \"Cartoon Planet,\" and related Cartoon Network productions using characters from the \"Space Ghost\" series.\n- C. Martin Croker was best known for voicing Zorak and Moltar on the animated series \"Space Ghost Coast to Coast,\" replacing Don Messick.\n- \"Space Ghost's Musical Bar-B-Que\" features songs and skits by Space Ghost and his arch enemies Zorak and Brak.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "2c0d96ec-cefb-5521-9969-08bdee595e8d",
        "text": "Page: Space Ghost's Musical Bar-B-Que. Sentence: Featuring songs and skits by Space Ghost and his arch enemies Zorak and Brak.\nPage: Brak (character). Sentence: Brak is a fictional character and supervillain on the 1966 Hanna-Barbera animated series \"Space Ghost\", portrayed as a catlike alien space pirate trying to conquer the galaxy.\nPage: Andy Merrill. Sentence: Andy Ronald Merrill (born November 27, 1966 in Newark, Ohio) is an American television writer, producer and voice actor best known for his comedy voice portrayal of the character Brak on \"Space Ghost Coast to Coast\" and \"Cartoon Planet\", and other related productions from Cartoon Network utilizing characters from the \"Space Ghost\" series.\nPage: C. Martin Croker. Sentence: He was best known for having provided the voices of Zorak and Moltar on the animated series \"Space Ghost Coast to Coast\", replacing Don Messick, who originally voiced the characters in the 1960s series \"Space Ghost\".",
